# ---- Environment / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
# The negations are per-FILENAME, not per-prefix: `!.env.example` does not rescue
# `.env.prod.example`, which matches `.env.*` and would otherwise be written, never
# committed, and silently missing from the published repository. Every new committed
# template needs its own line here. Check with:
#     git check-ignore -v deployment/.env.prod.example     # must print nothing
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example

# ---- Python / uv (backend, T-003) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
# uv.lock IS committed — do not ignore it

# ---- Node / Vite (frontend, T-004) ----
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# T-510's fidelity screenshots are diagnostics for a human, never a baseline to diff against
# (R-66(5): a screenshot comparison is sensitive to font-load timing and subpixel antialiasing,
# and blurs exactly the errors the computed-property assertions state outright). Regenerate with
# `node fidelity/run.mjs`.
frontend/fidelity/screenshots/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `backend/openapi.json` and `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts` are generated and **committed**
# on purpose (T-405). Committing them means `npm run build` needs no Python, and a developer
# who changed a route without regenerating sees a dirty working tree — which, with no CI in
# this repo, is the only signal there is. A backend pytest guards the first against the app.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- Data / runtime artifacts ----
*.log
/tmp/
minio-data/
# Local-filesystem object-storage backend (STORAGE_BACKEND=local, T-201)
.data/
pgdata/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---- Private to this working copy (not published) ----
# Third-party / course-supplied source material — not ours to relicense under GPL-3.0.
ReferenceDocs/
RAG Chatbot GUI Design/
# Internal build board and phase plan.
planning/
# Authoritative specification (requirement IDs, rulings, open issues).
Nexus_AI_Detailed_Specification.md
# Agent orientation + project skills (reference the excluded docs above).
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
# Measurement corpora for a task in flight — third-party books and vendor manuals held only
# to measure a detector against (T-728 sized FR-ING-10's ratio on six of them). Same reason as
# ReferenceDocs/ above: not ours to relicense, and hundreds of megabytes nobody reviews.
.t728-samples/

# ---- Ad-hoc probe scripts at the repo root (NEVER commit) ----
# The root is where throwaway PowerShell probes land while driving a running stack by hand, and
# they routinely carry a live password inline (both of the ones this rule was written for do).
# Same backstop reasoning as the OAuth secret below — the window between writing one and
# deciding where it belongs is exactly when `git add -A` catches it. A script worth keeping goes
# under deployment/ or backend/tools/, which this pattern deliberately does not match.
/*.ps1

# ---- Third-party OAuth credentials (NEVER commit) ----
# Google Cloud Console hands you a `client_secret_*.json` containing a live
# `GOCSPX-` secret. Corpus needs it in **Keycloak only** (R-63: the backend stores no
# third-party credential), so the file has no business in this tree at all — this is a
# backstop for the window between downloading it and moving it somewhere safe.
client_secret_*.json
*client_secret*.json
credentials.json

# ---- Generated API reference (regenerate, never edit) ----
# `backend: python -m tools.apidocs` (pdoc) and `frontend: npm run docs` (TypeDoc) render these
# from docstrings already in the source. A generated file committed to the tree changes on every
# docstring edit, nobody reviews the diff, and it silently stops matching. docs/HTTP_API.md is
# the one deliberate exception -- it is committed WITH a drift test.
docs/reference/

# ---- Backup output (NEVER commit) ----
# `deployment/backup.sh` writes here by default. A backup directory holds a full pg_dump of
# BOTH databases -- every document, conversation and audit row, plus Keycloak's credential
# material -- and a byte-for-byte copy of every uploaded original. It is the single most
# sensitive artefact this repository can produce. Keep it off the host, not in the tree.
backups/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
